<title>FRANCE: BoF sold marks to support French franc - traders.</title>
<headline>BoF sold marks to support French franc - traders.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign exchange traders said on Thursday the Bank of France intervened in the market earlier this morning to support the French franc.</p>
<p>&quot;The Bank of France sold marks at 3.4295 at around nine o'clock (0700 GMT),&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>By 1120 GMT, the franc was at 3.4267/72 marks after hitting an intraday low of 3.4296 earlier.</p>
<p>The Bank of France declined comment on the reports as is its custom in such situations.</p>
</text>
